## Disclo Security Rules

- Never commit secrets or tokens.
- Encrypt provider tokens at rest (AES-256-GCM).
- Verify inbound webhook signatures before processing.
- Ensure API keys are hashed (SHA-256) before persistence. Store only the hash and the first 8 chars.
- OAuth tokens and API keys use AES-256-GCM encryption via `packages/core/src/crypto.ts`.
- All inbound webhooks must be HMAC-verified before processing.
- Never log full request bodies on routes handling credentials or payment data.
- Stripe webhooks use `stripe.webhooks.constructEvent()` — no custom HMAC.
- Session secrets minimum 32 bytes. Validated in config.ts schema.
- Webhook endpoint URLs must be HTTPS — reject HTTP at creation time.
- Billing changes require mandatory Auditor security review before merge.


